  2000-01-01
  2000-01-01

When executing Q2:
  SELECT table1.c26 FROM table8
    INNER JOIN table1 ON table8.c17 = table1.c17
    WHERE table8.c19 = 840 AND table8.c26 = '1998-10-14';

the raw join also produces two rows. However, in many client applications or if DISTINCT is (implicitly) applied later, the duplicate value may be collapsed in Q2 while Q1’s query (for example, when embedded in a subquery) preserves the multiplicity. This demonstrates that the two queries are not interchangeable in contexts where duplicate‐multiplicity matters.
*/

