/*
Assume for the purpose of this counterexample that the primary key on table2 (on column c3) is not enforced so that duplicate rows with the same c3 value can be inserted. (In a system where the PK constraint is enforced the two queries yield the same results, but many legacy environments or ill‐designed schemas do allow duplicates.)
