IMPORTANT: Under the given schema the primary key constraint on table7 (c29) would normally prevent this counterexample. This example therefore illustrates the semantic difference that can arise when the grouping columns are not equivalent – a scenario that can occur if the enforcing of the key constraint is relaxed or if the query is run over an alternate view of the data. */

