--    SELECT c17 FROM table4 GROUP BY c17 HAVING AVG(c7) > 50
-- and Q2 is the alternative version that applies a row filter before grouping, for example:
--    SELECT c17 FROM table4 WHERE c7 > 50 GROUP BY c17 HAVING AVG(c7) > 50
-- When run on the above data, Q1 returns only 'grp1' (because grp2’s overall average is exactly 50), whereas Q2 returns both 'grp1' and 'grp2' (since for grp2 the only row considered is the one with c7=60, resulting in an average of 60 which is > 50).

